        },
        {
          "name": "Archer",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Orléans, spring 1429",
      "narration": "Spring 1429. The city of Orléans has been surrounded by the English for six months. If it falls, the road into the heart of France lies open. And France is running out of hope.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-02",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 48,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-02.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Charles",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Its future king hides in a castle far to the south, short of money and short of friends. He hasn't even been crowned. Some days, he isn't sure he deserves to be.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-03",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 62,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-03.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "And then, out of nowhere, a teenage peasant girl appears and says that God has sent her to fix all of it.",
      "word_count": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-04",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 72,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-04.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Treaty of Troyes, 1420",
      "narration": "Remember the treaty after Agincourt? It made the English king the heir to France. And when Henry the Fifth and the French king both died in 1422, the English declared Henry's baby son king of both countries.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-05",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 88,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-05.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Burgundian knight",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Charles",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The English and their powerful allies, the Dukes of Burgundy, held Paris and most of the north. The French king's son, Charles, held the south. People called him the Dauphin, the heir, because he still hadn't been crowned.",
      "word_count": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-06",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 105,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-06.png",
      "background": "cathedral",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Reims",
      "narration": "French kings were crowned in the cathedral of Reims. But Reims was deep in enemy territory. And without a coronation, many people simply didn't see Charles as a real king.",
      "word_count": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-07",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "France on the brink",
      "start": 118,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-07.png",
      "background": "siege",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "In October 1428, the English laid siege to Orléans, the last great city guarding the road south. Month after month, it held on. Barely.",
      "word_count": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-08",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 129,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-08.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Mother",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Domrémy, around 1412",
      "narration": "Far to the east, in a village called Domrémy, lived a peasant girl named Jeanne. In English, Joan. Her family farmed, kept animals and went to church. She never learned to read or write.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-09",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 144,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-09.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "When she was about thirteen, Joan said she began to hear voices. She believed they came from saints, sent by God. At first, they simply told her to be good and to go to church.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-10",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 159,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-10.png",
      "background": "village",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Then, she said, the message changed. The voices told her to leave home, drive the English out of France, and take the Dauphin to Reims to be crowned.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-11",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 171,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-11.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Baudricourt",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Robert de Baudricourt",
      "narration": "At sixteen, she walked to the nearest garrison town and asked its captain, Robert de Baudricourt, for an escort to the Dauphin. He laughed, and told her family to take her home.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-12",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The girl from Domrémy",
      "start": 185,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-12.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Baudricourt",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "She came back. And kept coming back. Eventually, the captain gave in. According to one story, she had predicted a French defeat before the news of it even arrived.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-13",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 198,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-13.png",
