          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "bow"
        },
        {
          "name": "Courtier",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Chinon",
      "narration": "At the castle of Chinon, the story goes, Charles tested her. He hid among his courtiers while someone else took his place. Joan walked straight past the impostor and knelt in front of the real Dauphin.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-15",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 225,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-15.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "But Charles wasn't going to bet his kingdom on a story. For weeks, churchmen questioned Joan. They found nothing bad to say about her. And frankly, Charles was out of options.",
      "word_count": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-16",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Chinon",
      "start": 239,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-16.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"Forty times more than my sword\"",
      "narration": "So he gave her armor, a horse and a place with an army heading for Orléans. She carried a white banner covered in lilies. She later said she loved that banner forty times more than her sword.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
