          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Reims, 17 July 1429",
      "narration": "On the seventeenth of July 1429, Charles was crowned King of France in Reims Cathedral. Joan stood near the altar, holding her banner.",
      "word_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-27",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The crown at Reims",
      "start": 357,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-27.png",
      "background": "cathedral",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Joan",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "\"It had borne the burden\"",
      "narration": "Later, someone asked why her banner deserved a place at the ceremony. She answered: it had borne the burden, so it was right that it should have the honor.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-28",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Captured",
      "start": 370,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-28.png",
      "background": "hall",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
