          "name": "French knight",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "English knight",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "walk"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "1453: the war ends",
      "narration": "Joan didn't live to see it, but the war had turned. Over the next twenty years, the English lost almost everything they held in France except the port of Calais. In 1453, the Hundred Years' War was finally over.",
      "word_count": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-39",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 508,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-39.png",
      "background": "court",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Churchman",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "1456: declared innocent",
      "narration": "In 1456, a new church court reviewed her case and declared the first trial unjust. Joan was officially innocent, twenty-five years too late.",
      "word_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-40",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 518,
